Notes
-----
- The 2026-11-20 Reactive Resume live run used the deterministic planner for the
  model layer (no host-model credentials were available), not a real model call.
- On 2026-11-20 a real DeepSeek key (user-supplied, env vars only) verified the
  OpenAI-compatible adapter end-to-end: real /chat/completions -> Pydantic-valid
  JobRequirements -> analyzer invariants. WorkBuddy and DeepSeek Harness remain
  NOT live-verified; that run did not exercise them.
- The credential used was never written to disk or committed; only env vars were set.
- No real API key, token, personal resume, or PII is stored in this repository.
- Credentials are read from env vars or the user-level file ~/.offerbomber/credentials.json
  (outside the repo); explicit constructor args override both.
- Test count is from an actual `pytest -q` run: 171 passed, 1 skipped (2026-11-20), not a function count.
- Test suite: 110 prior + 29 Phase 3.3 security regressions + 32 Phase 4-6 general-agent tests
  (tests/test_phase46_general.py). The single skip is the real-Gmail send test, enabled only by
  explicit user authorization; no mock is counted as a real integration.
- Run `offerbomber model doctor`, `offerbomber status` and `offerbomber agent status` for CLI status.
- MCP human approval: Elicitation is deliberately NOT used. The MCP spec forbids
  form-mode elicitation for credentials and it is not a server-verifiable authorization
  signal; approval runs out-of-band in the local CLI instead.
- Streamable HTTP transport is NOT implemented; the server is stdio-only.
